            <ArticleTitle>Oral meptazinol--United Kingdom experience.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>29-34</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An oral formulation of meptazinol has been developed and marketed in the United Kingdom. The 200 mg tablet has a potency similar to dextropropoxyphene 32.5 mg/paracetamol 325 mg or pentazocine 50 mg. Nausea is the major side effect and constipation and dysphoria are virtually absent. Though a variable first pass metabolism restricts its potential for use in severe pain, oral meptazinol provides effective analgesia in mild or moderate pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
